From 1d2063448021ff94e1b18bb26e98936c7fb89a9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arnaldo Lima <arnaldolimaof@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:01:49 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] SPU on x86: SSE4.1 float ops, SSE4.1 for lifted code;
 timestamps for the frame chain

- spu_helpers.h: SSE4.1 forms of fa/fs/fm/fma/fms/fnms, the NEON path lane
  for lane as two f64x2 halves (lanes off the fast path go to the scalar
  path). On x86 every float op was four scalar lanes behind a call.
  tests/test_spu_float_neon.c now runs on SSE4.1 too: bit-identical to the
  references on 8M cases; fma+fm pair 41.9 -> 8.7 ns.
- templates/project: lifted SPU sources get -msse4.1 (probed). spu_shufb is
  pshufb only under __SSE4_1__; without it every shufb was a byte loop, a
  third of the job worker in God of War: Ascension.
- [atom-ea] commit lines, [ww] and [GET_REPORT] carry t=<us> on one clock
  (ps3_qpc_us), and the commit line prints the whole line after the store:
  enough to lay a frame's dependency chain out in time.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
